Rem Capability: file
Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedisam.shoddy — reckoner seed: isam.shoddy, whole-table words
Rem only, over a handle the CALLER already opened
Rem
Rem THIS SEED DOES NOT REGISTER ISAMOPEN. R3.5(b) is why: a handle must
Rem never reach the stack, because a handle is a NUMBER capped at 16 and
Rem shared with sockets, and UNDO after an open would restore the stack
Rem while leaving the handle open and now unreachable. So
Rem RckSeedIsamNum/RckSeedIsamStr take an ALREADY-OPEN Isam handle as
Rem their own argument — closed over inside the words they register,
Rem never pushed — the way a form field or an embedded scripting layer
Rem (R1.4's "equally its callers") would seed the engine with a table its
Rem host already knows about.
Rem
Rem "CANNOT" IS NOW TOO STRONG, and this comment used to say it.
Rem reckoner.shoddy holds resources by NAME, in a table UNDO does not
Rem touch, with CLOSE and BOUND over it — so "open a table from the
Rem entry line" no longer breaks R3.5(b) on its own, and a future
Rem ISAMOPEN would bind rather than push.
Rem
Rem WHAT STILL STOPS IT IS THE RECORD LAYOUT, which is a different
Rem problem and was always the harder half. An Isam carries Rd, Wr and
Rem KeyOf — reader, writer and key functions over the CALLER's own Type,
Rem written in Shoddy and compiled in. A host program has them. A
Rem session has to be told a layout at the prompt, which means a schema
Rem cell and generic functions driven by it. Until that exists this seed
Rem stays as it is, and the reason it stays is worth keeping straight:
Rem it is the layout, not the handle.
Rem
Rem TWO ENTRY POINTS, NOT ONE GENERIC ONE. isam.shoddy's keys must be
Rem NUMBERs or STRINGs (its own header comment says so), and Shoddy has
Rem no way to ask a Cell which of the two it holds and hand back a
Rem value of the matching generic type — so a NUMBER-keyed table seeds
Rem through RckSeedIsamNum and a STRING-keyed one through
Rem RckSeedIsamStr. Both register the same five words.
Rem
Rem RECORDS CROSS THE BRIDGE THROUGH cellOf, A FUNCTION THE CALLER
Rem SUPPLIES ( [ t -- Cell ] ), not a new stack case: isam's record type
Rem is the caller's own Type, unknown here exactly as it is unknown to
Rem isam.shoddy itself, and a PAIR built from field to field (as
Rem CSVPAIRS already does for a CSV row) is the usual shape to hand
Rem back. ISAMGETOR needs no inverse: its default argument is already a
Rem CELL as typed on the entry line, pushed back unchanged when the key
Rem is absent, never converted to or from the record type.
Rem
Rem WHOLE-TABLE WORDS ONLY (R3.5(b) again): ISAMALL, ISAMRANGE, ISAMHAS,
Rem ISAMGETOR and ISAMCOUNT. No BOPEN, no SEEK, no per-slot access.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "isam.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"

Rem ---- NUMBER-keyed tables ----------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedIsamNum(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    Let st1 = IsnSeedAll(RckSeeding(st, "seed-isam"), db, cellOf)
    Let st2 = IsnSeedCount(st1, db)
    Let st3 = IsnSeedHas(st2, db)
    Let st4 = IsnSeedRange(st3, db, cellOf)
    IsnSeedGetor(st4, db, cellOf)

Def IsnSeedAll(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMALL", 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutList(Map(IsamAll(db), cellOf)) })), "( -- list )", "Every record in the table, key order.")

Def IsnSeedCount(st As RckState, db As Isam) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMCOUNT", 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(IsamCount(db)) })), "( -- n )", "How many records the table holds.")

Def IsnSeedHas(st As RckState, db As Isam) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMHAS", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => IsnHas(db, vs)), "( k -- flag )", "Whether the table has a record under key k.")

Def IsnHas(db As Isam, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("ISAMHAS", First(vs))
        Case Ok(k)
            RckVals({ CutBool(IsamHas(db, k)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMHAS did not answer")

Def IsnSeedRange(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMRANGE", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => IsnRange(db, cellOf, vs)), "( lo hi -- list )", "The records with keys from lo to hi inclusive, key order.")

Def IsnRange(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("ISAMRANGE", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(lo)
            IsnRangeAt(db, cellOf, lo, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMRANGE did not answer")

Def IsnRangeAt(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], lo As Number, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("ISAMRANGE", c)
        Case Ok(hi)
            RckVals({ CutList(Map(IsamRange(db, lo, hi), cellOf)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMRANGE did not answer")

Def IsnSeedGetor(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMGETOR", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => IsnGetor(db, cellOf, vs)), "( k dflt -- rec )", "The record under key k, or dflt unchanged when there is none.")

Def IsnGetor(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("ISAMGETOR", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(k)
            RckVals({ IsnGetorAt(db, cellOf, k, Nth(vs, 2)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMGETOR did not answer")

Def IsnGetorAt(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], k As Number, dflt As Cell) As Cell
    If IsamHas(db, k) Then
        Call(cellOf, IsamGet(db, k))
    Else
        dflt

Rem ---- STRING-keyed tables ------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedIsamStr(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    Let st1 = IssSeedAll(RckSeeding(st, "seed-isam"), db, cellOf)
    Let st2 = IssSeedCount(st1, db)
    Let st3 = IssSeedHas(st2, db)
    Let st4 = IssSeedRange(st3, db, cellOf)
    IssSeedGetor(st4, db, cellOf)

Def IssSeedAll(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMALL", 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutList(Map(IsamAll(db), cellOf)) })), "( -- list )", "Every record in the table, key order.")

Def IssSeedCount(st As RckState, db As Isam) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMCOUNT", 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => RckVals({ CutNum(IsamCount(db)) })), "( -- n )", "How many records the table holds.")

Def IssSeedHas(st As RckState, db As Isam) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMHAS", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => IssHas(db, vs)), "( k -- flag )", "Whether the table has a record under key k.")

Def IssHas(db As Isam, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("ISAMHAS", First(vs))
        Case Ok(k)
            RckVals({ CutBool(IsamHas(db, k)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMHAS did not answer")

Def IssSeedRange(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMRANGE", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => IssRange(db, cellOf, vs)), "( lo hi -- list )", "The records with keys from lo to hi inclusive, key order.")

Def IssRange(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("ISAMRANGE", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(lo)
            IssRangeAt(db, cellOf, lo, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMRANGE did not answer")

Def IssRangeAt(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], lo As String, c As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("ISAMRANGE", c)
        Case Ok(hi)
            RckVals({ CutList(Map(IsamRange(db, lo, hi), cellOf)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMRANGE did not answer")

Def IssSeedGetor(st As RckState, db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ]) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMGETOR", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => IssGetor(db, cellOf, vs)), "( k dflt -- rec )", "The record under key k, or dflt unchanged when there is none.")

Def IssGetor(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("ISAMGETOR", Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(k)
            RckVals({ IssGetorAt(db, cellOf, k, Nth(vs, 2)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMGETOR did not answer")

Def IssGetorAt(db As Isam, cellOf As [ t -- Cell ], k As String, dflt As Cell) As Cell
    If IsamHas(db, k) Then
        Call(cellOf, IsamGet(db, k))
    Else
        dflt

Rem ======================================================================
Rem A TABLE A SESSION OPENS FOR ITSELF
Rem
Rem Everything above takes a table the HOST already opened. This half
Rem takes a path and a schema typed at the prompt, and is what the
Rem "cannot" at the top of this file used to rule out.
Rem
Rem TWO THINGS HAD TO EXIST FIRST, and neither is a better guard.
Rem reckoner.shoddy now holds resources by NAME in a table UNDO does not
Rem touch, so an open table is reachable after any number of undos and
Rem no handle goes on the stack. And seedrecio.shoddy worked out how to
Rem describe a record layout at a prompt — a list of { name kind }
Rem specs — which is the half R3.5(b) never had anything to say about,
Rem and the half that actually kept isam out.
Rem
Rem THE SCHEMA LANGUAGE IS SEEDRECIO'S, not a second dialect. This file
Rem includes that seed and calls its reader, its writer and its row
Rem checks, so the two record machines cannot drift into disagreeing
Rem about what a spec means. That is why seedrecio is among this seed's
Rem dependencies: one definition, used twice.
Rem
Rem ---- THE ONE PLACE THE TYPES FIGHT BACK ----------------------------
Rem
Rem isam orders keys with a raw "<", so KeyOf's answer must be a NUMBER
Rem or a STRING at the TYPE level. CutLess exists but answers a CutCalc
Rem rather than a Boolean, so a Cell key will not do. The schema that
Rem says WHICH is data, read at run time.
Rem
Rem So there are two instantiations of Isam here, held in one sum type
Rem and chosen when the schema is read. Every word branches on that sum
Rem once and then does the same thing on either side. It reads like
Rem duplication and it is not: the two sides have different types, and
Rem that is exactly the fact the language is stating.
Rem
Rem THE ISAM IS REBUILT ON EVERY CALL from the two handles the binding
Rem carries. That is sound because isam's own mutators say so — each
Rem returns the now-unchanged handle — so every byte of state lives in
Rem the two files, and an Isam is a record of two handles, a size and
Rem three functions this seed supplies. IsamOpen's one-time work,
Rem initialising a fresh index or rebuilding a stale one, happens at
Rem ISAMOPEN and never again.
Rem
Rem EVERY WORD PRE-FLIGHTS, because isam Errors rather than refusing:
Rem IsamInsert on a duplicate key, IsamUpdate, IsamDelete and IsamGet on
Rem a missing one. IsamHas and IsamCount answer all of those questions
Rem first, so nothing here can end a session.
Rem ======================================================================

Include "seedrecio.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"
Include "str.shoddy"

Rem ---- the two instantiations, and the sum that holds either -----------

Type IsamHeld = IsamByNum(HeldNum As Isam) | IsamByStr(HeldStr As Isam)

Def IskKindName() As String
    "isam"

Rem Which position in the schema the key field sits at, or 0 for a key
Rem naming no field at all.
Def IskKeyAt(fs As List Of RecField, key As String, k As Number) As Number
    If k > Length(fs) Then
        0
    Else
        IskKeyIs(fs, key, k)

Def IskKeyIs(fs As List Of RecField, key As String, k As Number) As Number
    If RfName(Nth(fs, k)) = key Then
        k
    Else
        IskKeyAt(fs, key, k + 1)

Rem ---- reading and writing a record, in isam's own shape ---------------

Rem isam hands its reader a handle it has already sought, exactly as
Rem recio does, so seedrecio's field walk serves unchanged.
Def IskRd(fs As List Of RecField, f As Number) As Cell
    CutList(RcReadFields(f, fs, { }))

Def IskWr(fs As List Of RecField, f As Number, rec As Cell)
    RcWriteFields(f, fs, IskCellsOf(rec))

Def IskCellsOf(rec As Cell) As List Of Cell
    Select Case rec
        Case CutList(xs)
            xs
        Case Else
            { }

Def IskKeyNumOf(at As Number, rec As Cell) As Number
    IskNumOf(Nth(IskCellsOf(rec), at))

Def IskKeyStrOf(at As Number, rec As Cell) As String
    IskStrOf(Nth(IskCellsOf(rec), at))

Def IskNumOf(c As Cell) As Number
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            x
        Case Else
            0

Def IskStrOf(c As Cell) As String
    Select Case c
        Case CutStr(s)
            s
        Case Else
            ""

Rem ---- the binding's own data cell -------------------------------------

Rem The data handle, the index handle, the record size, the schema as
Rem the session typed it, and the key's position. The two handles are
Rem here rather than on the stack, which is the whole of what makes this
Rem safe: reachable by name, unreachable by value.
Def IskDataCell(fh As Number, ih As Number, size As Number, sc As Cell, at As Number) As Cell
    CutList({ CutNum(fh), CutNum(ih), CutNum(size), sc, CutNum(at) })

Def IskPart(r As RckRes, k As Number) As Cell
    Nth(IskCellsOf(ResDataOf(r)), k)

Def IskFh(r As RckRes) As Number
    IskNumOf(IskPart(r, 1))

Def IskIxFh(r As RckRes) As Number
    IskNumOf(IskPart(r, 2))

Def IskSize(r As RckRes) As Number
    IskNumOf(IskPart(r, 3))

Def IskSchemaCell(r As RckRes) As Cell
    IskPart(r, 4)

Def IskKeyPos(r As RckRes) As Number
    IskNumOf(IskPart(r, 5))

Rem ---- rebuilding the table a word was named ---------------------------

Def IskHeld(r As RckRes, fs As List Of RecField) As IsamHeld
    If FldKind(Nth(fs, IskKeyPos(r))) = RcNumKind() Then
        IsamByNum(Isam(IskFh(r), IskIxFh(r), IskSize(r), Fn(f) => IskRd(fs, f), Fn(f, v) => IskWr(fs, f, v), Fn(v) => IskKeyNumOf(IskKeyPos(r), v)))
    Else
        IsamByStr(Isam(IskFh(r), IskIxFh(r), IskSize(r), Fn(f) => IskRd(fs, f), Fn(f, v) => IskWr(fs, f, v), Fn(v) => IskKeyStrOf(IskKeyPos(r), v)))

Def IskFound(word As String, st As RckState, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckTextArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(nm)
            IskFoundAt(word, st, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def IskFoundAt(word As String, st As RckState, nm As String) As Result
    If Not RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        Err(word & ": THERE IS NOTHING OPEN CALLED " & nm, 0)
    Else
        IskFoundKind(word, First(RckResOf(st, nm)), nm)

Def IskFoundKind(word As String, r As RckRes, nm As String) As Result
    If ResKindOf(r) <> IskKindName() Then
        Err(word & ": " & nm & " IS A " & Upper(ResKindOf(r)) & ", NOT A TABLE", 0)
    Else
        Ok(r)

Def IskSchemaFor(word As String, r As RckRes) As Result
    RcSchemaOf(word, IskSchemaCell(r))

Rem ---- ISAMOPEN ---------------------------------------------------------

Def IskSeedOpen(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "ISAMOPEN", 4, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskOpen(s, vs)), "( path schema key name -- )", "Open an indexed table and keep it open under that name. The schema is a list of { name kind } specs, as for RECOPEN, and key names which field is the key. Makes the table if it is not there. CLOSE shuts it; BOUND lists what is open.")

Def IskOpen(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckTextArg("ISAMOPEN", Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("ISAMOPEN", Nth(vs, 4)))
        Case Pair(Ok(path), Ok(nm))
            IskOpenFree(st, path, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3), nm)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN needs a path, a schema, a key field and a name")

Def IskOpenFree(st As RckState, path As String, sc As Cell, kc As Cell, nm As String) As RckWork
    If RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN: THERE IS ALREADY SOMETHING OPEN CALLED " & nm)
    Else
        IskOpenKey(path, sc, kc, nm)

Def IskOpenKey(path As String, sc As Cell, kc As Cell, nm As String) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("ISAMOPEN", kc)
        Case Ok(key)
            IskOpenSchema(path, sc, key, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN did not answer")

Def IskOpenSchema(path As String, sc As Cell, key As String, nm As String) As RckWork
    Select Case RcSchemaOf("ISAMOPEN", sc)
        Case Ok(fs)
            IskOpenFound(path, sc, key, nm, fs, IskKeyAt(fs, key, 1))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN did not answer")

Rem A key naming no field is the mistake worth catching hardest: the
Rem table would otherwise be built around a position that is not there.
Def IskOpenFound(path As String, sc As Cell, key As String, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number) As RckWork
    If at = 0 Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN: NO FIELD IS CALLED " & key & " — THE SCHEMA HAS " & Join(RcNames(fs), " "))
    Else
        IskOpenOrdered(path, sc, nm, fs, at)

Rem The key must be a NUMBER or a STRING because isam keeps keys in
Rem order. A BOOLEAN key would compile and would give a table that can
Rem hold two records, which is a worse outcome than a refusal.
Def IskOpenOrdered(path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number) As RckWork
    If FldKind(Nth(fs, at)) = RcBoolKind() Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN: THE KEY FIELD " & RfName(Nth(fs, at)) & " IS A BOOLEAN — A KEY MUST BE A NUMBER OR A STRING, BECAUSE THE TABLE KEEPS THEM IN ORDER")
    Else
        IskOpenMade(path, sc, nm, fs, at)

Def IskOpenMade(path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number) As RckWork
    If Not FileExists(path) And Not TryWriteFile(path, "") Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN: CANNOT MAKE '" & path & "'")
    Else
        IskOpenNow(path, sc, nm, fs, at, RcSize(fs))

Rem IsamOpen goes through BOpen, which ABORTS on a path it cannot use.
Rem TryBOpen is asked first purely as the pre-flight: if the data file
Rem opens, it is shut again at once and isam is left to do its own
Rem opening, index rebuild and all.
Def IskOpenNow(path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number, size As Number) As RckWork
    Select Case TryBOpen(path)
        Case Ok(probe)
            IskOpenProbed(RcShut(probe), path, sc, nm, fs, at, size)
        Case Err(w, where)
            RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN did not answer")

Def IskOpenProbed(shut As Boolean, path As String, sc As Cell, nm As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number, size As Number) As RckWork
    If FldKind(Nth(fs, at)) = RcNumKind() Then
        IskOpenedAs(IsamByNum(IsamOpen(path, size, Fn(f) => IskRd(fs, f), Fn(f, v) => IskWr(fs, f, v), Fn(v) => IskKeyNumOf(at, v))), sc, nm, at)
    Else
        IskOpenedAs(IsamByStr(IsamOpen(path, size, Fn(f) => IskRd(fs, f), Fn(f, v) => IskWr(fs, f, v), Fn(v) => IskKeyStrOf(at, v))), sc, nm, at)

Def IskOpenedAs(h As IsamHeld, sc As Cell, nm As String, at As Number) As RckWork
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            RckOpened(nm, IskKindName(), Fh(db), IskDataCell(Fh(db), IxFh(db), RecSize(db), sc, at), Fn() => IskShut(Fh(db), IxFh(db)))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            RckOpened(nm, IskKindName(), Fh(db), IskDataCell(Fh(db), IxFh(db), RecSize(db), sc, at), Fn() => IskShut(Fh(db), IxFh(db)))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMOPEN did not answer")

Rem A table is TWO files, so the closer shuts two handles. The core sees
Rem one resource under one name, which is what a session should see too.
Def IskShut(fh As Number, ih As Number) As Boolean
    BClose(fh)
    BClose(ih)
    True

Rem ---- the branch, once per operation -----------------------------------

Rem Each of these is the same call written twice over two different key
Rem types. There is no way to write it once: the two Isam values do not
Rem share a type, and a generic helper would have to name the key type
Rem it was generic over.

Def IskCountOf(h As IsamHeld) As Number
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IsamCount(db)
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IsamCount(db)
        Case Else
            0

Def IskHasOf(h As IsamHeld, kc As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IsamHas(db, IskNumOf(kc))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IsamHas(db, IskStrOf(kc))
        Case Else
            False

Def IskGetOf(h As IsamHeld, kc As Cell) As Cell
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IsamGet(db, IskNumOf(kc))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IsamGet(db, IskStrOf(kc))
        Case Else
            CutList({ })

Def IskAllOf(h As IsamHeld) As List Of Cell
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IsamAll(db)
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IsamAll(db)
        Case Else
            { }

Def IskRangeOf(h As IsamHeld, lo As Cell, hi As Cell) As List Of Cell
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IsamRange(db, IskNumOf(lo), IskNumOf(hi))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IsamRange(db, IskStrOf(lo), IskStrOf(hi))
        Case Else
            { }

Rem The mutators answer the handle they were given, unchanged, so their
Rem answer is taken and dropped: everything they did is in the files.
Def IskInsertOf(h As IsamHeld, rec As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IskDid(IsamInsert(db, rec))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IskDid(IsamInsert(db, rec))
        Case Else
            False

Def IskUpdateOf(h As IsamHeld, rec As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IskDid(IsamUpdate(db, rec))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IskDid(IsamUpdate(db, rec))
        Case Else
            False

Def IskDeleteOf(h As IsamHeld, kc As Cell) As Boolean
    Select Case h
        Case IsamByNum(db)
            IskDid(IsamDelete(db, IskNumOf(kc)))
        Case IsamByStr(db)
            IskDid(IsamDelete(db, IskStrOf(kc)))
        Case Else
            False

Def IskDid(db As Isam) As Boolean
    True

Rem ---- what a key must be, asked before it is used ----------------------

Rem IskNumOf answers 0 for anything that is not a NUMBER and IskStrOf
Rem answers "" for anything that is not a STRING, so an unchecked key of
Rem the wrong kind would not fail — it would quietly look up the wrong
Rem record. That is the one failure mode worth the most care here.
Def IskWhyKey(word As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number, kc As Cell) As String
    If FldKind(Nth(fs, at)) = RcNumKind() Then
        IskWhyNum(word, fs, at, kc)
    Else
        IskWhyStr(word, fs, at, kc)

Def IskWhyNum(word As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number, kc As Cell) As String
    Select Case kc
        Case CutNum(x)
            ""
        Case Else
            word & ": THE KEY " & RfName(Nth(fs, at)) & " IS A NUMBER, AND THAT IS NOT ONE"

Def IskWhyStr(word As String, fs As List Of RecField, at As Number, kc As Cell) As String
    Select Case kc
        Case CutStr(s)
            ""
        Case Else
            word & ": THE KEY " & RfName(Nth(fs, at)) & " IS A STRING, AND THAT IS NOT ONE"

Rem A whole row, checked against the schema exactly as RECPUT checks
Rem one — same schema language, same checker, same messages.
Def IskWhyRec(word As String, fs As List Of RecField, rec As Cell) As String
    Select Case RckListArg(word, rec)
        Case Ok(xs)
            IskWhyWide(word, fs, xs)
        Case Err(w, at)
            w
        Case Else
            word & " did not answer"

Def IskWhyWide(word As String, fs As List Of RecField, xs As List Of Cell) As String
    If Length(xs) <> Length(fs) Then
        word & ": THE RECORD HAS " & Str(Length(xs)) & " VALUES AND THE SCHEMA HAS " & Str(Length(fs)) & " FIELDS"
    Else
        RcWhyRow(word, xs, fs, 1)

Rem ---- the words -------------------------------------------------------

Rem Every one of them starts the same way: a name off the stack, the
Rem binding, its schema, and the table rebuilt from the two handles the
Rem binding carries.

Def IskSeedCount(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "ISAMCOUNT", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskCount(s, vs)), "( name -- n )", "How many records the table bound under that name holds.")
    RckReg(s1, "ISAMFIELDS", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskFields(s, vs)), "( name -- list )", "The field names of that table's schema, in the order a record lists them. The key is one of these.")

Def IskCount(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMCOUNT", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            RckVals({ CutNum(IskCountOf(IskHeldOf(p))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMCOUNT did not answer")

Def IskFields(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMFIELDS", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            RckVals({ CutList(Map(RcNames(IskFieldsOf(p)), CutStr)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMFIELDS did not answer")

Def IskSeedHas(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "ISAMHAS", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskHas(s, vs)), "( name k -- flag )", "Whether the table has a record under key k.")
    RckReg(s1, "ISAMGETOR", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskGetor(s, vs)), "( name k dflt -- rec )", "The record under key k as a list of values in schema order, or dflt unchanged when there is none. There is no plain ISAMGET: a missing key would have nothing to answer with.")

Def IskHas(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMHAS", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            IskHasKeyed("ISAMHAS", p, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMHAS did not answer")

Def IskHasKeyed(word As String, p As IsamUse, kc As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskWhyKey(word, IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), kc) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(IskWhyKey(word, IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), kc))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutBool(IskHasOf(IskHeldOf(p), kc)) })

Def IskGetor(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMGETOR", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            IskGetorKeyed(p, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMGETOR did not answer")

Rem IsamGet Errors on a missing key, so the presence check is not a
Rem convenience — it is the whole reason this word is reachable.
Def IskGetorKeyed(p As IsamUse, kc As Cell, dflt As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskWhyKey("ISAMGETOR", IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), kc) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(IskWhyKey("ISAMGETOR", IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), kc))
    Else
        RckVals({ IskGetorAt(IskHeldOf(p), kc, dflt) })

Def IskGetorAt(h As IsamHeld, kc As Cell, dflt As Cell) As Cell
    If IskHasOf(h, kc) Then
        IskGetOf(h, kc)
    Else
        dflt

Def IskSeedAll(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "ISAMALL", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskAll(s, vs)), "( name -- list )", "Every record in the table, in key order, each one a list of values in schema order.")
    RckReg(s1, "ISAMRANGE", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskRange(s, vs)), "( name lo hi -- list )", "Every record whose key lies from lo to hi, in key order.")

Def IskAll(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMALL", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(p)
            RckVals({ CutList(IskAllOf(IskHeldOf(p))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMALL did not answer")

Def IskRange(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMRANGE", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            IskRangeKeyed(p, Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMRANGE did not answer")

Def IskRangeKeyed(p As IsamUse, lo As Cell, hi As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskWhyKey("ISAMRANGE", IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), lo) & IskWhyKey("ISAMRANGE", IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), hi) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(IskWhyEither("ISAMRANGE", p, lo, hi))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutList(IskRangeOf(IskHeldOf(p), lo, hi)) })

Def IskWhyEither(word As String, p As IsamUse, lo As Cell, hi As Cell) As String
    If IskWhyKey(word, IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), lo) <> "" Then
        IskWhyKey(word, IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), lo)
    Else
        IskWhyKey(word, IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), hi)

Def IskSeedWrite(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "ISAMINSERT", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskInsert(s, vs)), "( name rec -- )", "Add rec to the table. Refuses when a record with that key is already there — ISAMUPDATE is the one that replaces.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "ISAMUPDATE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskUpdate(s, vs)), "( name rec -- )", "Replace the record with rec's key. Refuses when there is none — ISAMINSERT is the one that adds.")
    RckReg(s2, "ISAMDELETE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => IskDelete(s, vs)), "( name k -- )", "Remove the record under key k. Refuses when there is none.")

Def IskInsert(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMINSERT", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            IskInsertRow(p, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMINSERT did not answer")

Rem Two pre-flights, and isam Errors on either: the row has to fit the
Rem schema, and the key has to be absent.
Def IskInsertRow(p As IsamUse, rec As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskWhyRec("ISAMINSERT", IskFieldsOf(p), rec) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(IskWhyRec("ISAMINSERT", IskFieldsOf(p), rec))
    Else
        IskInsertFree(p, rec, IskKeyIn(p, rec))

Def IskInsertFree(p As IsamUse, rec As Cell, kc As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskHasOf(IskHeldOf(p), kc) Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMINSERT: THERE IS ALREADY A RECORD UNDER THAT KEY — ISAMUPDATE REPLACES ONE")
    Else
        IskWrote(IskInsertOf(IskHeldOf(p), rec))

Def IskUpdate(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMUPDATE", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            IskUpdateRow(p, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMUPDATE did not answer")

Def IskUpdateRow(p As IsamUse, rec As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskWhyRec("ISAMUPDATE", IskFieldsOf(p), rec) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(IskWhyRec("ISAMUPDATE", IskFieldsOf(p), rec))
    Else
        IskUpdateThere(p, rec, IskKeyIn(p, rec))

Def IskUpdateThere(p As IsamUse, rec As Cell, kc As Cell) As RckWork
    If Not IskHasOf(IskHeldOf(p), kc) Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMUPDATE: THERE IS NO RECORD UNDER THAT KEY — ISAMINSERT ADDS ONE")
    Else
        IskWrote(IskUpdateOf(IskHeldOf(p), rec))

Def IskDelete(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case IskWith("ISAMDELETE", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(p)
            IskDeleteKeyed(p, Nth(vs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("ISAMDELETE did not answer")

Def IskDeleteKeyed(p As IsamUse, kc As Cell) As RckWork
    If IskWhyKey("ISAMDELETE", IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), kc) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(IskWhyKey("ISAMDELETE", IskFieldsOf(p), IskAtOf(p), kc))
    Else
        IskDeleteThere(p, kc)

Def IskDeleteThere(p As IsamUse, kc As Cell) As RckWork
    If Not IskHasOf(IskHeldOf(p), kc) Then
        RckWorkBad("ISAMDELETE: THERE IS NO RECORD UNDER THAT KEY")
    Else
        IskWrote(IskDeleteOf(IskHeldOf(p), kc))

Rem The write happened for its effect; the Boolean is how it is made to
Rem happen in a position where an answer can be given.
Def IskWrote(did As Boolean) As RckWork
    If did Then
        RckVals({ })
    Else
        RckVals({ })

Def IskKeyIn(p As IsamUse, rec As Cell) As Cell
    Nth(IskCellsOf(rec), IskAtOf(p))

Rem ---- what every word needs, gathered once -----------------------------

Rem The binding, its schema, the key's position and the rebuilt table.
Rem Assembling these four separately at every call site was the first
Rem draft and it read as noise; they always travel together.
Type IsamUse
    UseFields As List Of RecField
    UseAt     As Number
    UseHeld   As IsamHeld

Def IskFieldsOf(p As IsamUse) As List Of RecField
    UseFields(p)

Def IskAtOf(p As IsamUse) As Number
    UseAt(p)

Def IskHeldOf(p As IsamUse) As IsamHeld
    UseHeld(p)

Def IskWith(word As String, st As RckState, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case IskFound(word, st, c)
        Case Ok(r)
            IskWithSchema(word, r)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def IskWithSchema(word As String, r As RckRes) As Result
    Select Case IskSchemaFor(word, r)
        Case Ok(fs)
            Ok(IsamUse(fs, IskKeyPos(r), IskHeld(r, fs)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem ---- the seed ---------------------------------------------------------

Rem The entry point a mill folds with no arguments, unlike
Rem RckSeedIsamNum/RckSeedIsamStr above, which need a table their host
Rem already opened. A mill folds one or the other: the word NAMES are
Rem shared on purpose, so a session learns one vocabulary, and the
Rem arities differ because these take the name of the table to work on.
Def RckSeedIsam(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = IskSeedOpen(RckSeeding(st, "seed-isam"))
    Let s2 = IskSeedCount(s1)
    Let s3 = IskSeedHas(s2)
    Let s4 = IskSeedAll(s3)
    IskSeedWrite(s4)
